WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.120
Welcome to Grade 2 English, Unit 3: Ready, Steady, Go!

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:05.560
Get ready to move!

3
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:14.180
In this unit you learn the names of the parts of your body,
and lots of action words such as hop, jump, clap and wave.

4
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:18.200
You follow movement instructions
and then give commands of your own.

5
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:25.300
You also learn how to stay healthy and strong by moving
every day, eating good food, drinking water and sleeping well.

6
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:33.000
By the end you can say what someone is doing right now,
just like Amal and her friends in this unit's story,

7
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.120
“The Big Race”.

8
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.020
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:45.720
By the end of this unit, you will be able to
identify and name different parts of your body.

10
00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:49.420
You will also understand and use action words about movement.

11
00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:53.040
You will also follow simple movement instructions in English.

12
00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:55.940
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:03.100
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: keep, boot, cool, cook, pull, push.

14
00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:08.540
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

15
00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:13.740
The reading sequence includes A Poem: “Reach for the Sky!”

16
00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:15.640
and Healthy and Strong.

17
00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:21.400
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

18
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:25.560
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

19
00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:30.540
The first language focus is Giving Commands (Imperatives).

20
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:33.760
A command tells someone what to do.

21
00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:39.460
We use commands to give movement instructions
in a game, in an exercise or at a race.

22
00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:44.280
Learning commands helps you follow your
teacher and lead an action game yourself.

23
00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:49.000
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

24
00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:54.020
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 — Naming Body Parts.

25
00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:57.420
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

26
00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:04.520
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

27
00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:06.200
You are ready to begin.

28
00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:12.280
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

29
00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:19.200
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
